# Docs screenshot: vector edit mode (docs/editor/vector-edit.md, #45) - an
# ellipse with a radial gradient and a rectangle drawn with Edit Art.
wait 5
key escape
click @hier.add
type vector
click @addnode.create
wait 2
click @insp.vec.draw
wait 2
click @vd.tool:ellipse
drag @node:VectorShape+-60,-90 @node:VectorShape+60,30
click @vd.style.fill.kind
click @pick:Radial gradient
click @vd.tool:rect
drag @node:VectorShape+-40,30 @node:VectorShape+40,140
click @vd.tool:select
drag @node:VectorShape+-90,-110 @node:VectorShape+90,160
wait 3
annotate @vd.tool:pen Tools: select, nodes, pen, shapes, pencil, brush, bucket, eyedropper, gradient
annotate @vd.def.fillColor Fill, line colour and width of new shapes
annotate @vd.convert Selected shapes to a symbol (F8)
annotate @vd.done Done (Esc)
annotate @vd.style.for Layers and the shape's fill / stroke in the Inspector
screenshot editor_vector-edit
click @window:viewport
key f1
expect noderef.page == editor/vector-edit
